    "status": "present",
    "value": "Decide whether two encoded strings can represent a common original, allowing digit runs to split into positive wildcard lengths. The approach is: memoized two-string positions plus unmatched wildcard-length balance; enumerate all digit-run partitions. Its target cost is O(n*m*D) reachable states/time up to constant digit branching; O(n*m*D) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
